cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Zero-DSP FPGA inference findings, please cite this work. Pure LUT-based ternary inference requires 0 DSP blocks."
title: "Trinity B002: Zero-DSP FPGA Architecture for Ternary Neural Inference"
abstract: "We present a complete FPGA architecture for ternary neural network inference requiring zero DSP blocks. Key innovations include: (1) Zero-DSP ternary MAC using pure LUT arithmetic; (2) CORDIC sacred routing with 6-stage continued fraction approximation; (3) Streaming argmax unit (<100 LUT); (4) Ternary BRAM storage with 2-bit packed weights; (5) Power-of-2 embedding lookup for cache efficiency; (6) Ternary scheduler with φ-weighted round-robin; (7) ESP32 Wi-Fi JTAG for cross-platform programming; (8) OpenXC7 synthesis pipeline (Yosys → nextpnr → Bitstream). Results: 19.6% LUT utilization, 0% DSP usage, 1.2W power consumption on XC7A100T. Pure Zig → Verilog workflow with Docker-based reproducibility. Complete MLSys reproducibility card with resource utilization breakdown and synthesis timing analysis."
